## Runtime adapter facts

Find custom profiles in project `.cursor/agents/` or user `~/.cursor/agents/`; a file on disk is not discovery proof, so inspect the live catalog. CLI, App local, and App Cloud are separate hosts. Materialize the selected project explicitly. Cloud requires installation in its environment setup, a tested and user-saved Build, then a new top-level Agent in the same repository; local install never deploys Cloud.
Inspect the current `Task` schema and send only fields it exposes. If the exact Kaola role is present and its materialized profile receipt is valid, call `Task` with the live flat `subagent_type: "<role>"` field and MUST omit the per-call `model`; an exact-tier requirement is a post-resolution assertion, never authorization to populate that field. Absence of medium/high from the generic Task model enum is not a named-profile capability gap. Verify an exact tier from `providerOptions.cursor.modelName` provider evidence when the host exposes it; a TUI child transcript alone is insufficient. Internal `subagentType.custom.name` is provider encoding, not controller call shape, and must not be sent. In a built-in-only enum, omit-model is the parent, not a profile pin.

**Tier defaults:** standard — standard → profile `grok-4.6[effort=medium]`; reasoning — reasoning → profile `grok-4.6[effort=high]`; heavy — heavy → profile `grok-4.6[effort=xhigh]`.
**Role roster:** standard — `code-explorer`, `doc-updater`, `implementer`, `investigator`, `knowledge-lookup`, `metric-optimizer`, `tdd-guide`; reasoning — `adversarial-verifier`, `build-error-resolver`, `code-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `synthesizer`; heavy — `code-architect`, `planner`.

The named profile's native `readonly` flag carries its write boundary.
Inspect the live Task catalog. Measured hosts exposed writable `generalPurpose` and host-specific built-ins; some hosts document scoped `Explore`, `Bash`, or `Browser`. Use only a route this host reports, under its real identity and capability.
The live Task catalog is authoritative. CLI build 2026.08.25-3e8eec8 proved project `implementer` dispatch and resolved `cursor-grok-4.6-medium`; App 3.17.21 and the saved Cloud Build each proved all 14 names plus exact `implementer`, but did not expose the child model carrier. CLI profile reload was observed after reopening the process; same-process hot load remains unknown.

If the exact name is absent, first distinguish an uninstalled or unsaved host carrier from a capability gap. Then inspect real alternatives for this item; a custody-bearing miss inlines only that item and records the specific `capability_gap`.
